---
import DocPage from '../../components/company/DocPage.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../data/site';
import { LEGAL, LEGAL_DOCS, lastUpdatedLabel, missingIdentity } from '../../data/legal';

const crumbs = [{ label: 'Legal', href: '/legal/' }];
const status = LEGAL.reviewed ? 'Reviewed' : 'Draft — pending legal review';
---
<DocPage
  title="Legal information"
  metaTitle="Legal information"
  description="Index of the panoptes.watch legal documents — privacy notice, website terms of use and cookie notice — with their scope, review status and last-updated dates."
  eyebrow="Legal"
  lede="The documents that govern this website, what each one covers and when it last changed. They apply to the panoptes.watch website only; use of the Panoptes product is governed by a separate agreement with each customer."
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
  ogImage="/social/og-company.png"
  updated={lastUpdatedLabel}
  draft={!LEGAL.reviewed}
  placeholders={missingIdentity}
>
  <h2 id="website-documents">Website documents</h2>
  <p>These documents apply to everyone who visits panoptes.watch.</p>
  <ul class="legal-docs">
    {LEGAL_DOCS.map((d) => (
      <li class="card">
        <h3><Icon name={d.icon} /> <a href={d.href}>{d.title}</a></h3>
        <p>{d.scope}</p>
        <p class="ld-meta"><span>Last updated: {lastUpdatedLabel}</span><span>Status: {status}</span></p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>

  <h2 id="review-status">Review status</h2>
  {LEGAL.reviewed ? (
    <p>The documents listed above have been reviewed. Each shows the date it was last updated at the top of the page.</p>
  ) : (
    <p>All three documents are <strong>drafts pending legal review</strong>. They describe how this website actually works, but they have not yet been reviewed by legal counsel, and each one says so in a notice at the top of the page. Some company details, such as the registered company name and address, are still to be confirmed; until then the documents name the operator simply as “Panoptes”.</p>
  )}
  <p>When a document changes, its “last updated” date changes too. Earlier versions are not currently published on this site.</p>

  <h2 id="customer-agreements">Customer agreements and data processing terms</h2>
  <p>The documents above cover the website only. Access to and use of the Panoptes product is governed by a written agreement between Panoptes and each customer, including any terms for processing personal data on the customer’s behalf. These agreements are not published on this website.</p>
  <p>If you are evaluating Panoptes and want to discuss contractual or data processing terms, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.salesEmail}`}>{SITE.salesEmail}</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="security">Security information</h2>
  <p>How Panoptes approaches security and governance for the product — access control, data ownership, auditability and the decisions agreed with each customer during evaluation — is described on the <a href="/integrations/security-governance/">security and governance</a> page. How this website itself protects form submissions and restricts the resources pages may load is covered in the <a href="/privacy/#security">privacy notice</a>.</p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about any of these documents, or requests about your personal data: <a href={`mailto:${LEGAL.privacyEmail}?subject=Privacy`}>{LEGAL.privacyEmail}</a>. For privacy requests, please put “Privacy” in the subject line.</p>
</DocPage>

<style>
  .legal-docs { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 1.4em 0 0; display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
  .legal-docs li { margin: 0; padding: 1.2rem 1.4rem; }
  .legal-docs h3 { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin: 0 0 .5rem; font-size: 1.1rem; }
  .legal-docs h3 :global(svg) { width: 20px; height: 20px; flex: none; color: var(--accent-text); }
  .legal-docs p { margin: 0; }
  .ld-meta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .4rem 1.4rem; margin-top: .8rem !important; font: 500 .78rem/1.4 var(--font-mono); color: var(--text-3); }
</style>
